ReXGlue input: KeyboardMouseActive() for keyboard button prompts.

True while the keyboard/mouse device is the one that last gave player 1 real input (the active-device
rule the input system already keeps: a neutral pad never takes over). A game reads it to show key
pictures instead of pad buttons.

diff --git a/include/rex/input/pad_style.h b/include/rex/input/pad_style.h
index 6292ee5..dd4510f 100644
--- a/include/rex/input/pad_style.h
+++ b/include/rex/input/pad_style.h
@@ -13,4 +13,8 @@ enum class PadStyle : int { kNone = 0, kXbox = 1, kPlayStation = 2 };
 PadStyle ConnectedPadStyle();
 void SetConnectedPadStyle(PadStyle style);
 
+// True while keyboard/mouse is the device that last gave player 1 real input (a key, a mouse button: the same
+// rule that picks the active device), for keyboard prompts.
+bool KeyboardMouseActive();
+
 }  // namespace rex::input
diff --git a/src/input/input_system.cpp b/src/input/input_system.cpp
